# NOTE: Assertions are hand-written; they check -debug-only output, which
# NOTE: utils/update_mir_test_checks.py does not generate.
# REQUIRES: asserts
# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgpu9.08 -run-pass=machine-scheduler -amdgpu-disable-unclustered-high-rp-reschedule -amdgpu-remat-extend-deps -verify-machineinstrs %S/machine-scheduler-remat-extend-deps.mir -o /dev/null -debug-only=machine-scheduler,gcn-rematerialization-strategy 2>&1 | FileCheck -check-prefix=EXTEND %s
# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgpu9.08 -run-pass=machine-scheduler -amdgpu-disable-unclustered-high-rp-reschedule -amdgpu-remat-extend-deps=false -verify-machineinstrs %S/machine-scheduler-remat-extend-deps.mir -o /dev/null -debug-only=machine-scheduler,gcn-rematerialization-strategy 2>&1 | FileCheck -check-prefix=NOEXTEND %s

# Shows how the pre-RA rematerialization stage reaches its pressure target in
# machine-scheduler-remat-extend-deps.mir. The final MIR only shows the
# rematerialized registers; the intermediate steps are only visible in the
# stage's debug output.
#
# In extend_shared_base, region 1 starts at 15/12 VGPRs. Each rematerialized
# address saves one VGPR. The first one extends the live range of %base through
# regions 0 to 2, which costs one VGPR in each of them; this is charged to the
# RP targets right away. The four addresses therefore reach the 12/12 target in
# a single round, without the estimate being too optimistic.
#
# In wide_dep_narrow_users, each 32-bit address would only save one VGPR while
# extending the 64-bit %base costs two, so the addresses are not candidates.

# EXTEND-LABEL: In function @extend_shared_base: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# EXTEND:       [1] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# EXTEND:       NEW REMAT ROUND
# EXTEND:       ** REMAT {{.*}}%addr0:vgpr_32 = V_ADD_U32_e32 0, %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:    [0] Extending %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:    [1] Extending %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:    [2] Extending %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:  ** REMAT {{.*}}%addr1:vgpr_32 = V_ADD_U32_e32 16, %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:  ** REMAT {{.*}}%addr2:vgpr_32 = V_ADD_U32_e32 32, %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:  ** REMAT {{.*}}%addr3:vgpr_32 = V_ADD_U32_e32 48, %base
# EXTEND-NEXT:    [1] Target reached!
# EXTEND-NOT:   Incorrect RP estimation
# EXTEND-NOT:   NEW REMAT ROUND
# EXTEND:       Objectives achieved!
# EXTEND:       REMAT RESULTS
# EXTEND:       [1] Achieved occupancy {{[0-9]+}}

# EXTEND-LABEL: In function @no_extend_across_blocks: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# EXTEND:       [0] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# EXTEND-NOT:   ** REMAT
# EXTEND:       Stop on exhausted rematerialization candidates

# EXTEND-LABEL: In function @wide_dep_narrow_users: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# EXTEND-NEXT:  Not extending dependencies of {{.*}}%addr0{{.*}}: their pressure exceeds the save
# EXTEND-NEXT:  Not extending dependencies of {{.*}}%addr1{{.*}}: their pressure exceeds the save
# EXTEND-NEXT:  Not extending dependencies of {{.*}}%addr2{{.*}}: their pressure exceeds the save
# EXTEND-NEXT:  Not extending dependencies of {{.*}}%addr3{{.*}}: their pressure exceeds the save
# EXTEND:       [1] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# EXTEND-NOT:   ** REMAT
# EXTEND:       Stop on exhausted rematerialization candidates

# NOEXTEND-LABEL: In function @extend_shared_base: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# NOEXTEND:       [1] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# NOEXTEND-NOT:   ** REMAT
# NOEXTEND:       Stop on exhausted rematerialization candidates

# NOEXTEND-LABEL: In function @no_extend_across_blocks: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# NOEXTEND:       [0] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# NOEXTEND-NOT:   ** REMAT
# NOEXTEND:       Stop on exhausted rematerialization candidates

# NOEXTEND-LABEL: In function @wide_dep_narrow_users: rematerializing to reduce spilling
# NOEXTEND-NOT:   Not extending
# NOEXTEND:       [1] Actual/Target: {{.*}}, 15/12 ArchVGPRs
# NOEXTEND-NOT:   ** REMAT
# NOEXTEND:       Stop on exhausted rematerialization candidates
